# Proposed config halving — NOT APPLIED
#
# The desk pricing spec (2026-05-12) flipped width semantics from
#   half-spread = mid * bps / 20000   (legacy: bid_w + ask_w = total spread)
# to
#   per-side offset = mid * bps / 10000   (current: each side gets the full bps)
#
# Under the new code, a config that still says bid_w = 20 / ask_w = 20 will
# quote a pair that is 40 bps apart on the venue, instead of the 20 bps the
# operator was getting under the old code. This patch HALVES every
#   width / bid_width / ask_width / width_bps
# key in `config/default_config.json` and `config/config.example.json` plus
# `desk_width_emergency_floor_bps` (6 → 3) in `config/config.example.json` so
# the on-venue spread under the NEW per-side bps semantics matches the
# on-venue spread that was being placed under the OLD half-spread semantics.
#
# Note: `config/default_config.json` does NOT currently declare
# `market_maker.desk_width_emergency_floor_bps`; the runtime falls back to the
# hard-coded default of 6 in `src/config/Config.cpp:1126`. If this halving is
# approved, the C++ default should be changed to 3 in a follow-up patch (or
# the key added to default_config.json with value 3).
#
# This patch is DO-NOT-AUTO-APPLY. To verify it would apply cleanly:
#   git apply --check proposed_config_halving.patch
# To apply once approved:
#   git apply proposed_config_halving.patch
#
